0001                               **************************************************
0002                               *                                                *
0003                               *               FORTH for the 6809               *
0004                               *                                                *
0005                               *    This version of FORTH was written to be     *
0006                               *    used as a ROM-able bare bones operating     *
0007                               *    system for a 6809 based micro-controller.   *
0008                               *    The high level defintions are based on      *
0009                               *    Thomas Newman's 8086/88 implementation of   *
0010                               *    the Forth Interest Group's model in order   *
0011                               *    to insure the portability of existing       *
0012                               *    code. All of the primitives were written    *
0013                               *    during July 1990 by:                        *
0014                               *                                                *
0015                               *                    Mike Pashea                 *
0016                               *          Southern Illinois University          *
0017                               *          Dept. of Engineering Box 1801         *
0018                               *          Edwardsville, Il. 62026-1801          *
0019                               *                  (618)-692-2391                *
0020                               *                                                *
0021                               *    This FORTH is direct threaded for speed,    *
0022                               *    however none of the assembly routines       *
0023                               *    have been optimized yet. It appears that    *
0024                               *    all of the bugs have been worked out        *
0025                               *    though.                                     *
0026                               *                                                *
0027                               *    The Forth Interest Group's publications     *
0028                               *    are public domain and may be obtained       *
0029                               *    from:                                       *
0030                               *                                                *
0031                               *            The Forth Interest Group            *
0032                               *            P.O. Box 1105                       *
0033                               *            San Carlos, Ca. 94070               *
0034                               *                                                *
0035                               *    The goal of this project has been to get    *
0036                               *    a small system up and running as quickly    *
0037                               *    as possible. The following source code      *
0038                               *    will assemble using the Motorola Freeware   *
0039                               *    6809 Assembler, with the number of          *
0040                               *    primitives being kept at a minimum.         *
0041                               *    Hopefully this will encourage translation   *
0042                               *    to similar Motorola processors, such as     *
0043                               *    the 68HC11. I've also commented the         *
0044                               *    primatives as much as possible to aid in    *
0045                               *    the translation.                            *
0046                               *                                                *
0047                               *    The target system for which this FORTH      *
0048                               *    was written has the following memory map:   *
0049                               *                                                *
0050                               *    0000-0400  A 2k EEPROM  (for saving code)   *
0051                               *    9800-9801  6850 ACIA    (serial port)       *
0052                               *    C000-DFFF  An 8k RAM    (FORTH dictionary,  *
0053                               *                             TIB and stacks)    *
0054                               *    E000-FFFF  An 8k ROM    (ROMable FORTH)     *
0055                               *                                                *
0056                               *    The current target system is being used     *
0057                               *    to develop other micro-controller systems   *
0058                               *    with EEPROM. Later hardware versions will   *
0059                               *    contain some parallel ports for doing data  *
0060                               *    aquisition and control.                     *
0061                               *                                                *
0062                               *    For the moment, there is no editor. In the  *
0063                               *    current system additional definitions are   *
0064                               *    written on an IBM PC and saved as an ascii  *
0065                               *    file. The definitions are then uploaded     *
0066                               *    through the serial port using Kermit. I     *
0067                               *    have written an assembler however, and      *
0068                               *    I'll give it out as soon as the bugs are    *
0069                               *    fixed.                                      *
0070                               *                                                *
0071                               *    FORTH Register Assignments                  *
0072                               *                                                *
0073                               *    FORTH  6809     FORTH Preservation Rules    *
0074                               *    -----  ----     ------------------------    *
0075                               *                                                *
0076                               *    IP      Y       INTERPRETER POINTER.        *
0077                               *                    MUST BE PRESERVED           *
0078                               *                    ACROSS FORTH WORDS.         *
0079                               *                                                *
0080                               *    W       X       WORD POINTER                *
0081                               *                                                *
0082                               *    SP      U       PARAMETER STACK POINTER.    *
0083                               *                    MUST BE PRESERVED ACROSS    *
0084                               *                    FORTH WORDS.                *
0085                               *                                                *
0086                               *    RP      S       RETURN STACK.               *
0087                               *                    MUST BE PRESERVED ACROSS    *
0088                               *                    FORTH WORDS.                *
0089                               *                                                *
0090                               *           RELEASE AND VERSION NUMBERS          *
0091                               *                                                *
0092                               **************************************************
0093 0001                          FIGREL  EQU   1
0094 0000                          FIGREV  EQU   0
0095 0000                          USRVER  EQU   0
0096                               
0097                               **************************************************
0098                               *                                                *
0099                               *            ASCII CHARACTERS USED               *
0100                               *                                                *
0101                               **************************************************
0102 0020                          ABL     EQU   $0020          ; A blank
0103 00d0                          ACR     EQU   $00D0          ; A carriage return
0104 002e                          ADOT    EQU   $002E          ; A period
0105 0007                          BELL    EQU   $0007          ; A bell (^G)
0106 005f                          BSIN    EQU   $005F          ; An input delete
0107 0008                          BSOUT   EQU   $0008          ; A output backspace
0108 0010                          DLE     EQU   $0010          ; (^P)
0109 00a0                          LF      EQU   $00A0          ; A line feed
0110 00c0                          FF      EQU   $00C0          ; A form feed
0111                               
0112                               **************************************************
0113                               *                                                *
0114                               *               MEMORY ALLOCATION                *
0115                               *                                                *
0116                               **************************************************
0117 c000                          RAMS    EQU   $C000          ; Start of RAM
0118 e000                          EM      EQU   $E000          ; End of RAM + 1
0119 0000                          NSCR    EQU   $0000          ; Number of 1024 byte screens
0120 0080                          KBBUF   EQU   $0080          ; Data bytes per disk buffer
0121 0040                          US      EQU   $0040          ; User variable space
0122 00a0                          RTS     EQU   $00A0          ; Return stack and terminal buffer
0123 0084                          CO      EQU   $0084          ; Data bytes per buffer plus 4
0124 0000                          NBUF    EQU   $0000          ; Number of buffers
0125 e000                          BUF1    EQU   $E000          ; First disk buffer
0126 dfc0                          INITR0  EQU   BUF1-US        ; Base of return stack
0127 df20                          INITS0  EQU   INITR0-RTS     ; Base of parameter stack
0128                               
0129 9800                          ACIAC   EQU   $9800          ; ACIA Control
0130 9801                          ACIAD   EQU   $9801          ; ACIA Data
0131                               
0132                               **************************************************
0133                               *                                                *
0134                               *             START OF ROMABLE FORTH             *
0135                               *                                                *
0136                               **************************************************
0137 e000                                  ORG   $E000
0138 e000 86 03              [ 2 ] ORIG    LDA   #$03           ; Configure the ACIA
0139 e002 b7 98 00           [ 5 ]         STA   ACIAC
0140 e005 86 16              [ 2 ]         LDA   #$16
0141 e007 b7 98 00           [ 5 ]         STA   ACIAC
0142 e00a 10 8e e0 19        [ 4 ]         LDY   #ENTRY
0143 e00e 10 ce df a0        [ 4 ]         LDS   #$DFA0         ; Initial stack pointers
0144 e012 ce df 20           [ 3 ]         LDU   #$DF20
0145 e015 ae a1              [ 8 ]         LDX   ,Y++           ; Set up is done, now do FORTH
0146 e017 6e 91              [ 9 ]         JMP   [,X++]
0147 e019 ef 2e                    ENTRY   FDB   COLD
0148                               
0149                               **************************************************
0150                               *                                                *
0151                               *                INITIAL USER TABLE              *
0152                               *                                                *
0153                               **************************************************
0154 e01b c0 12                    TOP     FDB   RTASK-7        ; Top word in FORTH vocabulary
0155 e01d df 20                    UTABLE  FDB   INITS0         ; Initial parameter stack base
0156 e01f df c0                            FDB   INITR0         ; Initial return stack base
0157 e021 df 20                            FDB   INITS0         ; Initial TIB
0158 e023 00 20                            FDB   32             ; Initial WIDTH
0159 e025 00 00                            FDB   0              ; Initial WARNING
0160 e027 c0 1d                            FDB   INITDP         ; Initial FENCE
0161 e029 c0 1d                            FDB   INITDP         ; Initial DP
0162 e02b c0 0e                            FDB   RFORTH+6       ; Initial VOC-LINK
0163 e02d df c0                    UP      FDB   INITR0         ; Initial user area pointer
0164 e02f df c0                    RPP     FDB   INITR0         ; Initial return stack pointer
0165                               
0166                               **************************************************
0167                               *                                                *
0168                               *           START OF THE FORTH DICTIONARY        *
0169                               *                                                *
0170                               **************************************************
0171 e031 83                       DP0     FCB   $83
0172 e032 4c 49                            FCC   'LI'
0173 e034 d4                               FCB   $D4            ; 'T'+$80
0174 e035 00 00                            FDB   $0000          ; LFA of zero indicates start of dictionary
0175 e037 e0 39                    LIT     FDB   *+2
0176 e039 ec a1              [ 8 ]         LDD   ,Y++           ; Get Literal
0177 e03b 36 06              [ 7 ]         PSHU  D              ; Push to user stack
0178 e03d ae a1              [ 8 ]         LDX   ,Y++           ; NEXT
0179 e03f 6e 91              [ 9 ]         JMP   [,X++]
0180                               
0181 e041 87                               FCB   $87
0182 e042 45 58 45 43 55 54                FCC   'EXECUT'
0183 e048 c5                               FCB   $C5
0184 e049 e0 31                            FDB   LIT-6
0185 e04b e0 4d                    EXEC    FDB   *+2
0186 e04d 37 10              [ 7 ]         PULU  X              ; Get CFA from parameter stack
0187 e04f 6e 91              [ 9 ]         JMP   [,X++]         ; Execute NEXT
0188                               
0189 e051 86                               FCB   $86
0190 e052 42 52 41 4e 43                   FCC   'BRANC'
0191 e057 c8                               FCB   $C8
0192 e058 e0 41                            FDB   EXEC-10
0193 e05a e0 5c                    BRAN    FDB   *+2
0194 e05c ec a4              [ 5 ] BRAN1   LDD   ,Y             ; Get offset value
0195 e05e 31 ab              [ 8 ]         LEAY  D,Y            ; Add offset to instruction pointer
0196 e060 ae a1              [ 8 ]         LDX   ,Y++           ; NEXT
0197 e062 6e 91              [ 9 ]         JMP   [,X++]
0198                               
0199 e064 87                               FCB   $87
0200 e065 30 42 52 41 4e 43                FCC   '0BRANC'
0201 e06b c8                               FCB   $C8
0202 e06c e0 51                            FDB   BRAN-9
0203 e06e e0 70                    ZBRAN   FDB   *+2
0204 e070 37 06              [ 7 ]         PULU  D
0205 e072 10 83 00 00        [ 5 ]         CMPD  #0             ; Is top of stack zero?
0206 e076 27 e4              [ 3 ]         BEQ   BRAN1          ; Yes, must branch
0207 e078 31 22              [ 5 ]         LEAY  2,Y            ; No, skip branch offset
0208 e07a ae a1              [ 8 ]         LDX   ,Y++           ; NEXT
0209 e07c 6e 91              [ 9 ]         JMP   [,X++]
0210                               
0211 e07e 86                               FCB   $86
0212 e07f 28 4c 4f 4f 50                   FCC   '(LOOP'
0213 e084 a9                               FCB   $A9
0214 e085 e0 64                            FDB   ZBRAN-10
0215 e087 e0 89                    XLOOP   FDB   *+2
0216 e089 cc 00 01           [ 3 ]         LDD   #$0001         ; Assume an increment of 1
0217 e08c e3 e4              [ 6 ] XLOO1   ADDD  0,S            ; Add increment to loop index
0218 e08e ed e4              [ 5 ]         STD   0,S            ; Put the new index on the stack
0219 e090 10 a3 62           [ 8 ]         CMPD  2,S            ; Compare index with limit
0220 e093 2d c7              [ 3 ]         BLT   BRAN1          ; Branch if index < limit
0221 e095 32 64              [ 5 ]         LEAS  4,S            ; Drop the index and the limit
0222 e097 31 22              [ 5 ]         LEAY  2,Y            ; Skip the branch offset
0223 e099 ae a1              [ 8 ]         LDX   ,Y++           ; NEXT
0224 e09b 6e 91              [ 9 ]         JMP   [,X++]
0225                               
0226 e09d 87                               FCB   $87
0227 e09e 28 2b 4c 4f 4f 50                FCC   '(+LOOP'
0228 e0a4 a9                               FCB   $A9
0229 e0a5 e0 7e                            FDB   XLOOP-9
0230 e0a7 e0 a9                    XPLOO   FDB   *+2
0231 e0a9 37 06              [ 7 ]         PULU  D              ; Get the increment value
0232 e0ab 20 df              [ 3 ]         BRA   XLOO1          ; Go do loop
0233                               
0234 e0ad 84                               FCB   $84
0235 e0ae 28 44 4f                         FCC   '(DO'
0236 e0b1 a9                               FCB   $A9
0237 e0b2 e0 9d                            FDB   XPLOO-10
0238 e0b4 e0 b6                    XDO     FDB   *+2
0239 e0b6 37 16              [ 9 ]         PULU  D,X            ; Get initial index and limit values
0240 e0b8 34 16              [ 9 ]         PSHS  X,D            ; Push to system stack
0241 e0ba ae a1              [ 8 ]         LDX   ,Y++           ; NEXT
0242 e0bc 6e 91              [ 9 ]         JMP   [,X++]
0243                               
0244 e0be 81                               FCB   $81
0245 e0bf c9                               FCB   $C9
0246 e0c0 e0 ad                            FDB   XDO-7
0247 e0c2 e0 c4                    IDO     FDB   *+2
0248 e0c4 ec e4              [ 5 ]         LDD   0,S            ; Get the index
0249 e0c6 36 06              [ 7 ]         PSHU  D              ; Push it to the parameter stack
0250 e0c8 ae a1              [ 8 ]         LDX   ,Y++           ; NEXT
0251 e0ca 6e 91              [ 9 ]         JMP   [,X++]
0252                               
0253 e0cc 85                               FCB   $85
0254 e0cd 44 49 47 49                      FCC   'DIGI'
0255 e0d1 d4                               FCB   $D4
0256 e0d2 e0 be                            FDB   IDO-4
0257 e0d4 e0 d6                    DIGIT   FDB   *+2
0258 e0d6 4f                 [ 2 ]         CLRA                 ; Clear high byte
0259 e0d7 e6 43              [ 5 ]         LDB   3,U            ; Ascii digit is low byte of 2nd on the stack
0260 e0d9 c0 30              [ 2 ]         SUBB  #$30           ; Convert to binary
0261 e0db 25 1b              [ 3 ]         BLO   DIGI2          ; Not a number
0262 e0dd c1 0a              [ 2 ]         CMPB  #$0A           ; Ascii 0-9?
0263 e0df 25 0a              [ 3 ]         BLO   DIGI1          ; Yes, check against base
0264 e0e1 c1 11              [ 2 ]         CMPB  #$11           ; Ascii A-Z?
0265 e0e3 25 13              [ 3 ]         BLO   DIGI2          ; No, less than 'A'
0266 e0e5 c1 2a              [ 2 ]         CMPB  #$2A
0267 e0e7 22 0f              [ 3 ]         BHI   DIGI2          ; No, greater than 'Z'
0268 e0e9 c0 07              [ 2 ]         SUBB  #7             ; Legal letter - convert to binary
0269 e0eb e1 41              [ 5 ] DIGI1   CMPB  1,U            ; Compare number to base (on top of stack)
0270                               
0271 e0ed 24 09              [ 3 ]                 BHS   DIGI2          ; Error if greater than or equal
0272 e0ef ed 42              [ 6 ]         STD   2,U            ; No error leave number on the stack
0273 e0f1 cc 00 01           [ 3 ]         LDD   #1             ; True flag
0274 e0f4 ed c4              [ 5 ]         STD   0,U            ; Put flag on top of stack
0275 e0f6 20 07              [ 3 ]         BRA   DIGI3          ; NEXT
0276 e0f8 33 42              [ 5 ] DIGI2   LEAU  2,U            ; Adjust stack
0277 e0fa cc 00 00           [ 3 ]         LDD   #0             ; False flag
0278 e0fd ed c4              [ 5 ]         STD   0,U            ; Put it on the stack
0279 e0ff ae a1              [ 8 ] DIGI3   LDX   ,Y++           ; NEXT
0280 e101 6e 91              [ 9 ]         JMP   [,X++]
0281                               
0282 e103 86                               FCB   $86
0283 e104 28 46 49 4e 44                   FCC   '(FIND'
0284 e109 a9                               FCB   $A9
0285 e10a e0 cc                            FDB   DIGIT-8
0286 e10c e1 0e                    PFIND   FDB   *+2
0287 e10e 34 20              [ 7 ]         PSHS  Y              ; Save IP
0288 e110 37 10              [ 7 ]         PULU  X              ; LFA of first word in the dictionary search
0289 e112 10 ae c4           [ 6 ] PFIN1   LDY   0,U            ; Location of packed string (HERE)
0290 e115 e6 84              [ 4 ]         LDB   0,X            ; Get dictionary word length
0291 e117 1f 98              [ 6 ]         TFR   B,A            ; Save the length byte temporarily
0292 e119 c4 3f              [ 2 ]         ANDB  #$3F           ; Mask off the two highest bits
0293 e11b e1 a4              [ 4 ]         CMPB  0,Y            ; Compare it with the packed string
0294 e11d 26 24              [ 3 ]         BNE   PFIN5          ; Lengths don't match - get another word
0295 e11f 30 01              [ 5 ] PFIN2   LEAX  1,X            ; OK so far - look at the text
0296 e121 31 21              [ 5 ]         LEAY  1,Y            ;
0297 e123 e6 84              [ 4 ]         LDB   0,X            ; Get next character
0298 e125 e1 a4              [ 4 ]         CMPB  0,Y            ; Compare with packed string
0299 e127 27 f6              [ 3 ]         BEQ   PFIN2          ; OK so far - go on to next character
0300 e129 c4 7f              [ 2 ]         ANDB  #$7F           ; Doesn't match - toggle high bit
0301 e12b e1 a4              [ 4 ]         CMPB  0,Y            ; Try again
0302 e12d 26 16              [ 3 ]         BNE   PFIN6          ; Doesn't match - go get next word
0303 e12f 30 05              [ 5 ] PFIN3   LEAX  5,X            ; We have an exact match - get PFA
0304 e131 1f 89              [ 6 ]         TFR   A,B            ; Retrieve length byte
0305 e133 4f                 [ 2 ]         CLRA                 ; D now contains the string length byte
0306 e134 af c4              [ 5 ]         STX   0,U            ; Replace location of packed string with PFA
0307 e136 8e 00 01           [ 3 ]         LDX   #1             ; Boolean TRUE flag
0308 e139 36 06              [ 7 ]         PSHU  D              ; Put string length on the stack
0309 e13b 36 10              [ 7 ]         PSHU  X              ; Put boolean flag on the stack
0310 e13d 35 20              [ 7 ] PFIN4   PULS  Y              ; Restore IP
0311 e13f ae a1              [ 8 ]         LDX   ,Y++           ; NEXT
0312 e141 6e 91              [ 9 ]         JMP   [,X++]
0313 e143 30 01              [ 5 ] PFIN5   LEAX  1,X            ; Skip character count
0314 e145 6d 80              [ 8 ] PFIN6   TST   0,X+           ; Test sign bit
0315 e147 2a fc              [ 3 ]         BPL   PFIN6          ; Keep looking - sign bit is not set
0316 e149 ae 84              [ 5 ] PFIN7   LDX   0,X            ; Get LFA
0317 e14b 8c 00 00           [ 4 ]         CMPX  #0             ; If zero we're at the end of the dictionary
0318 e14e 26 c2              [ 3 ]         BNE   PFIN1          ; Look at next word - LFA in X
0319 e150 af c4              [ 5 ]         STX   0,U            ; Put a boolean false on the stack
0320 e152 20 e9              [ 3 ]         BRA   PFIN4          ; NEXT
0321                               
0322 e154 87                               FCB   $87
0323 e155 45 4e 43 4c 4f 53                FCC   'ENCLOS'
0324 e15b c5                               FCB   $C5
0325 e15c e1 03                            FDB   PFIND-9
0326 e15e e1 60                    ENCL    FDB   *+2
0327 e160 34 20              [ 7 ]         PSHS  Y              ; Save the IP
0328 e162 37 06              [ 7 ]         PULU  D              ; Terminator character is now in B
0329 e164 ae c4              [ 5 ]         LDX   0,U            ; Get starting address, but keep it on the stack
0330 e166 10 8e ff ff        [ 4 ]         LDY   #-1            ; Set counter
0331 e16a 30 1f              [ 5 ]         LEAX  -1,X           ; Decrement starting address
0332 e16c 31 21              [ 5 ] ENCL1   LEAY  1,Y            ; Increment counter
0333 e16e 30 01              [ 5 ]         LEAX  1,X            ; Increment address
0334 e170 e1 84              [ 4 ]         CMPB  0,X            ; Is character a terminator?
0335 e172 27 f8              [ 3 ]         BEQ   ENCL1          ; Yes, continue looking
0336 e174 36 20              [ 7 ]         PSHU  Y              ; Character must be text, so push count offset
0337 e176 6d 84              [ 6 ]         TST   0,X            ; Is the character a NULL?
0338 e178 26 06              [ 3 ]         BNE   ENCL2          ; No, continue
0339 e17a 1f 21              [ 6 ]         TFR   Y,X            ; Copy counter
0340 e17c 31 21              [ 5 ]         LEAY  1,Y            ; Increment counter
0341 e17e 20 14              [ 3 ]         BRA   ENCL5          ; Do the push, get IP and do NEXT
0342 e180 31 21              [ 5 ] ENCL2   LEAY  1,Y            ; Increment counter
0343 e182 30 01              [ 5 ]         LEAX  1,X            ; Increment address
0344 e184 e1 84              [ 4 ]         CMPB  0,X            ; Is the character a terminator?
0345 e186 27 08              [ 3 ]         BEQ   ENCL4          ; Yes, finish up
0346 e188 6d 84              [ 6 ]         TST   0,X            ; No, is it a NULL?
0347 e18a 26 f4              [ 3 ]         BNE   ENCL2          ; No, continue looking
0348 e18c 1f 21              [ 6 ] ENCL3   TFR   Y,X            ; Counters are equal
0349 e18e 20 04              [ 3 ]         BRA   ENCL5          ; Do the push
0350 e190 1f 21              [ 6 ] ENCL4   TFR   Y,X            ; Copy counter
0351 e192 30 01              [ 5 ]         LEAX  1,X            ; Increment the counter
0352 e194 36 30              [ 9 ] ENCL5   PSHU  Y,X            ; Do the push
0353 e196 35 20              [ 7 ]         PULS  Y              ; Restore IP
0354 e198 ae a1              [ 8 ]         LDX   ,Y++           ; NEXT
0355 e19a 6e 91              [ 9 ]         JMP   [,X++]
0356                               
0357 e19c 84                               FCB   $84
0358 e19d 45 4d 49                         FCC   'EMI'
0359 e1a0 d4                               FCB   $D4
0360 e1a1 e1 54                            FDB   ENCL-10
0361 e1a3 e4 e4                    EMIT    FDB   DOCOL
0362 e1a5 f1 a4                            FDB   PEMIT
0363 e1a7 e5 61                            FDB   ONE
0364 e1a9 e6 3f                            FDB   OUTT
0365 e1ab e4 40                            FDB   PSTOR
0366 e1ad e3 0d                            FDB   SEMIS
0367                               
0368 e1af 83                               FCB   $83
0369 e1b0 4b 45                            FCC   'KE'
0370 e1b2 d9                               FCB   $D9
0371 e1b3 e1 9c                            FDB   EMIT-7
0372 e1b5 e4 e4                    KEY     FDB   DOCOL
0373 e1b7 f1 79                            FDB   PKEY
0374 e1b9 e3 0d                            FDB   SEMIS
0375                               
0376 e1bb 89                               FCB   $89
0377 e1bc 3f 54 45 52 4d 49                FCC   '?TERMINA'
     4e 41
0378 e1c4 cc                               FCB   $CC
0379 e1c5 e1 af                            FDB   KEY-6
0380 e1c7 e4 e4                    QTERM   FDB   DOCOL
0381 e1c9 f1 8b                            FDB   PQTER
0382 e1cb e3 0d                            FDB   SEMIS
0383                               
0384 e1cd 82                               FCB   $82
0385 e1ce 43                               FCC   'C'
0386 e1cf d2                               FCB   $D2
0387 e1d0 e1 bb                            FDB   QTERM-12
0388 e1d2 e4 e4                    CR      FDB   DOCOL
0389 e1d4 e0 37                            FDB   LIT
0390 e1d6 00 0d                            FDB   $0D
0391 e1d8 f1 a4                            FDB   PEMIT
0392 e1da e0 37                            FDB   LIT
0393 e1dc 00 0a                            FDB   $0A
0394 e1de f1 a4                            FDB   PEMIT
0395 e1e0 e3 0d                            FDB   SEMIS
0396                               
0397 e1e2 85                               FCB   $85
0398 e1e3 43 4d 4f 56                      FCC   'CMOV'
0399 e1e7 c5                               FCB   $C5
0400 e1e8 e1 cd                            FDB   CR-5
0401 e1ea e1 ec                    CMOVE   FDB   *+2
0402 e1ec 34 20              [ 7 ]         PSHS  Y              ; Save the instruction pointer
0403 e1ee 37 06              [ 7 ]         PULU  D              ; Get the count
0404 e1f0 e3 c4              [ 6 ]         ADDD  0,U            ; Add it to the destination address
0405 e1f2 37 30              [ 9 ]         PULU  X,Y            ; Destination in X, Source in Y
0406 e1f4 36 06              [ 7 ]         PSHU  D              ; Put final destination addr. on stack
0407 e1f6 a6 a0              [ 6 ] CMOV1   LDA   ,Y+            ; Do the move
0408 e1f8 a7 80              [ 6 ]         STA   ,X+
0409 e1fa ac c4              [ 6 ]         CMPX  0,U            ; At the final destination?
0410 e1fc 2d f8              [ 3 ]         BLT   CMOV1          ; If not, continue
0411 e1fe 33 42              [ 5 ]         LEAU  2,U            ; Drop final destination from the stack
0412 e200 35 20              [ 7 ]         PULS  Y              ; Restore the instruction pointer
